杰西卡  你现在
Jessica, you are now

81
00:06:48,860 --> 00:06:51,320
-是个货真价实的超级  -别说英开头的那个词
- a full-blown super- - Do not say the H-word.

82
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:54,270
-杰西  -我已经够头疼了
- Jess... - I-I've got enough of a headache as it is.

83
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,510
我就是说  你该考虑回趟家
I'm just saying, you might wanna consider going home,

84
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:59,130
睡会儿觉  然后再回归社会
getting some sleep, rejoining society.

85
00:06:59,130 --> 00:07:00,160
我这不跟你说话呢嘛
I'm talking to you.

86
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:02,200
我很感激
And I appreciate that.

87
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,970
-这里面是有威士忌吗  -是啊  那杯是我的
- Is there whiskey in this? - Oh, yeah, that's mine.

88
00:07:36,970 --> 00:07:39,160
看来你鼓捣文件没白忙活
Looks like all of your paper-pushing worked.

89
00:07:40,900 --> 00:07:44,020
给这位明星解开  把他带走
Uncuff the superstar. Get him out of my sight.

90
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:55,700
我不好
My bad.

91
00:07:58,490 --> 00:07:59,460
这是你的
These belong to you.

92
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:18,480
卢卡斯先生  凯奇先生
Mr. Lucas? Mr. Cage?

93
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:21,840
-你喜欢哪个来着  我忘了  -凯奇
- Which do you prefer? I forget. - Cage.

94
00:08:23,540 --> 00:08:25,900
-我认识你吗  -富兰克林·尼尔森
- Do I know you? - Franklin Nelson.

95
00:08:26,370 --> 00:08:30,130
我负责你的案子  我们经常通电话
I ran point on your case. We spoke on the phone... A lot.

96
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,789
是你经常说话
