只要好使就成
As long as it worked.

98
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:36,840
-多谢  -感谢你朋友波比·菲什吧
- I appreciate it. - Appreciate your friend Bobby Fish.

99
00:08:37,159 --> 00:08:39,330
我们都完成了不少工作
We all did some impressive book-cracking.

100
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,919
而且  你在监狱困难时期
Plus, you made it through a prison stint

101
00:08:41,929 --> 00:08:43,380
没有动过粗
without throwing a single punch.

102
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:44,940
我相信这不容易  考虑到你的...
I'm sure that was hard for a person with your...

103
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:47,010
-我知道  -名声
- I know. - ...reputation.

104
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:50,910
-克莱尔会来吗  -这里只有律师能进
- Is, uh... Claire coming? - It's lawyers only in here.

105
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:54,530
那失陪  我还得去赶大巴
Well, if you'll excuse me, I have a bus to catch.

106
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:57,650
当然  还有一件事
Of course. Uh, just one last thing.

107
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:01,620
霍加斯-赵-班诺维茨事务所随时为您服务
The law firm of Hogarth, Chao & Benowitz is at your disposal.

108
00:09:01,860 --> 00:09:03,420
如果您需要重新开始
In case you need help starting over.

109
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,000
我不会重新开始  尼尔森先生
I'm not starting over, Mr. Nelson.

110
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,340
我要向前看
I'm moving forward.

111
00:09:09,140 --> 00:09:10,400
大家喊我福吉
People call me Foggy.

112
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:11,910
你就默许了
And you let them?

113
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,410
您是公开声明  50街和10街交叉口的
You're on record as saying that the new subway station

114
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:24,720
地铁站会是  "对社区有利的"
at 50th and 10th would be, quote, "Good for the community."

115
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:28,510
会是...引述  "对社区有利的"
Would be quote-- quote, unquote, "Good for the community."

116
00:09:28,510 --> 00:09:31,920
博科威兹先生  以您专业...
Mr. Berkowitz, in your professional-

117
00:09:34,550 --> 00:09:35,510
你在干什么
What the hell are you doing?

118
00:09:35,590 --> 00:09:37,480
你干什么  看我爆了你的头
'Sup, man? I'll bust your goddamn head!

119
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,690
-是吗  来啊  -想干什么
- Oh, yeah? Let's go, then. - What's up?

120
00:09:39,690 --> 00:09:42,500
-想来挑衅一下吗  -来啊  上啊
- You wanna try something? - Come at me. Let's go!

121
00:09:44,550 --> 00:09:47,150
纽约警局  散开  够了
NYPD! Break it up! That's enough.

122
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:50,340
-你  人行道上的  -是  长官
- You, up on the sidewalk. - Yes, sir, officer.

123
00:09:54,090 --> 00:09:55,050
博科威兹先生
Mr. Berkowitz...

124
00:09:55,050 --> 00:09:57,740
以您专业的意见  这对亚伦·詹姆斯好吗
In your professional opinion, was it good for Aaron James?

125
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:59,190
我们同情他们一家
Our sympathies go out to the family.

126
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:00,790
但这件事  是个不幸
The whole thing... It's very unfortunate.

127
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,680
您可知道您新地铁站用的产品
Were you aware the products used in your new station

128
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:03,660
对儿童有害吗
were hazardous to children?

129
00:10:03,660 --> 00:10:05,020
-反对  -我重说
- Objection! - I'll rephrase.

130
00:10:05,020 --> 00:10:06,730
恩德萨本有什么优势
What was attractive about Endexoprene?

131
00:10:06,730 --> 00:10:08,440
强韧  持久
It's strong. It's durable.

132
00:10:08,450 --> 00:10:10,680
-价钱是别的一半  -我毕竟是做生意的
- And half the price? - Well, I do run a business.

133
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:13,970
为了省钱  就值得危害别人吗
Is it worth endangering people in the interest of saving money?

134
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:16,350
所有材料经过了测试
All materials are tested.

135
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,840
那些发现一被公布
The moment those findings were made public,

136
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:20,670
我们公司立刻换掉了其他所有站台的灰浆
our company replaced that mortar in all remaining stations.

137
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:22,590
"一被公布"
"Made public."

138
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:26,000
什么意思
What do you mean?

139
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:30,610
你是指9月29日公布的一份报告吗
Are you referring to a report released on September 29th?

140
00:10:30,610 --> 00:10:31,870
法官大人  他在要求我的委托人
Your Honor, he's asking my client

141
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:34,030
做出不合理的详尽回答
to respond with unreasonable specificity.

142
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,660
博科威兹先生  如果我没记错
Mr. Berkowitz, if memory serves me right,

143
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:37,120
您办公室于6月3日就收到了一份
your office received an urgent delivery

144
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,200
来自安全委员会的急件
from the Safety Commission on June 3rd.

145
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:40,160
那是三个月前
Three months earlier.

146
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:42,360
我好奇  那是否跟恩德萨本有任何关系
I'm curious, did that have anything to do with Endexoprene?

147
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,330
我毫不知情
I don't know anything about that.

148
00:10:43,330 --> 00:10:44,610
法官大人  默多克先生
Your Honor, unless Mr. Murdock

149
00:10:44,610 --> 00:10:45,620
若能证明我的委托人
can prove my client

150
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:48,050
真的收到了这些假设存在的文件  那
actually received these hypothetical documents, then--

151
00:10:48,050 --> 00:10:49,080
重点不是收没收到
It's not about whether he received them.

152
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:50,880
而是他是否有意无视了它
It's whether he willfully ignored them.

153
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,330
法官大人  我要求将这份送达记录
Your Honor, I ask that this record of delivery

154
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:53,560
收录证据
be admitted into evidence.

155
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:56,380
-我经常收到这玩意  -哪样最糟
- I mean, I get a lot of those. - What would you say is worse?

156
00:10:56,610 --> 00:10:58,600
为节省成本而无视数据
Ignoring data in the interest of cutting costs?

157
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:00,240
还是没有向法庭提交
Or neglecting to supply the court with records

158
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,320
或许能证明你有意危及他人生命的证据
that might prove you purposely put people in danger?

159
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,470
-包括这位年轻人  -法官大人
- Including this young man - Your Honor--

160
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:04,490
包括这位年轻人
Including this young man,

161
00:11:04,490 --> 00:11:06,360
亚伦·詹姆斯  他可能再也无法走路
Aaron James, who might never walk again.

162
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,250
法官大人  我们想请求休庭
Your Honor, we would like a recess.

163
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:09,490
不需要  我说完了
No need. I'm done.

164
00:11:10,350 --> 00:11:11,610
我觉得他也完了
I think he is, too.

165
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:23,440
一千一百万
$11 million!

166
00:11:24,290 --> 00:11:25,640
谢谢你  默多克先生
Thank you, Mr. Murdock.

167
00:11:25,650 --> 00:11:27,360
-不客气  -谢谢
- Oh, my pleasure. - Thank you.

168
00:11:27,760 --> 00:11:29,100
我很为你高兴
I'm so happy for you.

169
00:11:33,370 --> 00:11:34,350
天呐
God.

170
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,870
-你还好吧  -嗯
- You okay? - Yeah.

171
00:11:48,190 --> 00:11:49,540
我能跟你说句话吗
Mind if I tell you something?

172
00:11:50,590 --> 00:11:51,380
当然
Sure.

173
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,700
那钱对你父母会有很大帮助
That money is really gonna help your parents.

174
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:59,500
但对于你  从今往后
But for you, from here on out...

175
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:01,760
只会越来越难  亚伦
it's only gonna get harder, Aaron.

176
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:05,580
要知道你现在是在马拉松的第一英里
You realize you're only at mile one of the marathon...

177
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:07,700
你知道吧
right?

178
00:12:08,990 --> 00:12:10,830
每个人都会告诉你该有怎样的感受
Everybody's gonna tell you how to feel.

179
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:13,520
医生会告诉你保持积极
Doctors are gonna tell you to stay positive.

180
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,410
你的家人会告诉你不要自怨自艾
Your family's gonna tell you not to feel sorry for yourself.

181
00:12:15,410 --> 00:12:17,460
你的治疗师会告诉你别生气
Your therapist is gonna tell you not to be angry--

182
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:19,030
我已经生气了
I'm already angry.

183
00:12:20,090 --> 00:12:20,970
气谁
At who?

184
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:24,810
每一个人
Everyone.

185
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,790
我只想要回我的生活
I just want my life back.

186
00:12:29,530 --> 00:12:30,720
那是别人给不了的
They can't give you that.

187
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:34,890
或许你会再站起来
Maybe you'll walk again.

188
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:36,820
我希望能
I hope so.

189
00:12:38,710 --> 00:12:39,810
但或许你不会
But maybe you won't.

190
00:12:41,130 --> 00:12:45,340
但随着生活越来越难  如果你还能撑下来
But your ability to get through it... as this gets harder...

191
00:12:46,510 --> 00:12:48,060
那比强颜欢笑
that is a hundred times more powerful

192
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,710
假装一切都好
than slapping a smile on your face

193
00:12:49,710 --> 00:12:51,470
要强大千百倍
and pretending like everything's just fine.

194
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:55,070
你明白吗
Do you understand?

195
00:12:59,210 --> 00:12:59,890
听着
Listen...

196
00:13:00,810 --> 00:13:02,880
没有人能把你的生活还给你  亚伦
no one can give you your life back, Aaron.

197
